        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "Unable to explain anything",
                "difficulty_rating": 1,
                "quality_rating": 1
            },
            {
                "comment": "I took this class the semester I was leaving with a masters. really enjoyed it and learned a great deal. more than any other class in my two years there. it almost made me want to do research in AI and computer vision.  if you are average at math, skip this class.  there are three big homeworks and paper reviews each week. plus a research project. ",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Enthusiastic teacher but unhelpful outside of class (he talks but it's never useful or direct), rambles on during class and doesn't take into account the workload of students from other classes (assigns endless number of difficult homeworks). I would not take any course with him, just wait until another professor is teaching them.",
                "difficulty_rating": 5,
                "quality_rating": 2
            },
            {
                "comment": "Great instructor! I took CS540 at UW-Madison as a senior in high school and I still received an A even though I spent most of my time focusing on my high school classes. He was passionate about the topic and was a very nice guy. His slides are the same as his predecessors who taught 540 with some small variation. Great class overall, very valuable.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "This class needs LOT of work on programming and math. I barely managed a B. But what Vikes covers is very useful. Two questions on my interview at a tech startup were very similar to the ones on the final exam. I'm on the job for about six months now!!!",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "this is not an easy class and needs a LOT of work. i loved the second half of 540 (after logic). The svm and perceptron stuff is really really good but very mathy. if you already have a 1-2 semesters of calculus you'll do well. Many grad students take this class, so an A may be hard.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "He's a very nice person and really wants to help students. But his lectures are confusing and his lecture slides don't explain anything explicitly. There are not enough practice problems to prepare for exams either. One of the most frustrating classes.",
                "difficulty_rating": 5,
                "quality_rating": 3
            },
            {
                "comment": "Very nice person, and he really wants to help students understand. But his explanation is not clear and I was lost so many times in class. There were not enough practice problems to prepare you for the final. One of the most frustrating classes.",
                "difficulty_rating": 5,
                "quality_rating": 3
            },
            {
                "comment": "Nice guy, helpful outside of class, but lectures are sometimes very difficult to follow and rambly. Homeworks are very long and difficult. Midterm was reasonable difficult, final absurdly difficult. Choose a different professor if you really want to take this AI.",
                "difficulty_rating": 5,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "cs540 is a tough course regardless of who teaches it.  don't expect an easy A.  class is not curved and you will spend a good amount of time on HW (20-40 hrs)  you are expected to compete with some graduate students in the class too.  Vikas is actually very helpful, willing to slow down and explain things or make himself available outside of class.",
                "difficulty_rating": 5,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Very nice guy and very helpful outside of class. Lectures are sometimes a little rambly. However, he'll always stop to answer questions or slow down if asked. Seems to care about the class a lot. Textbook is totally useless and not even worth buying. I didn't use it at all.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "I have to say this was one of the most disappointing classes I've ever taken. Vikas' has his head in the right place as he's enthusiastic and very nice but his teaching leaves a lot to be desired. His lectures consist of him rambling and his online notes leave a lot to be desired. No practice exams or problems. Final exam was incredibly difficult",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 2
            }
